WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:02.402
Harry Kersh: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.837
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:06.206
between Wingstop in the UK and the US.

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:07.741
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:15.482
In the UK, we can get wing
portions in four sizes.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:17.784
Eight wings,

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:21.087
10 wings,

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.555
12 wings,

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.925
or a Flavour Craver wing platter,

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.696
which comes with 24 wings and three dips.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.464
US Wingstop, you can get your wings

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.700
in 10,

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.201
15,

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.269
ooh,

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.004
20,

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.472
[grunts]

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.473
30!

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:43.376
Hang on. And...

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.577
30.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.346
Not enough, you say? I agree.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:49.115
Wingstop also does wings in orders of...

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.519
50,

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:56.156
[laughing] 75,

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.892
and, of course,

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:04.164
100 chicken wings.

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.365
I'm in heaven right now.

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.467
Bury me in these wings.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:09.736
I'm going in.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:16.176
Eh, I could do better,
but we gotta move on.

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.745
Sean Evans, I'm coming for you, buddy.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.380
So, the portion sizes
might be pretty different,

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.948
but what about the wings themselves?

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.983
We're gonna weigh 10 plain wings in the UK

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.118
and do the same in the US

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.653
to see how they match up.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.623
So, 10 plain wings in
the UK came to 290 grams,

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.759
which is an average of 29 grams per wing.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.630
Joe: Oh, way higher, dude.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.732
360 grams.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.035
I needed my calculator app to determine

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.637
what 360 divided by 10 is.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:47.407
And it is, in fact, 36 grams.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:48.374
- Wow!
- So our average

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.710
is 36 grams per wing here in the US.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.811
What about chicken tenders?

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.347
Well, in the UK, those
come in two portion sizes:

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.015
as a portion of three

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:59.352
or as a portion of five.

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.287
At a Wingstop in the US, you
can get your chicken tenders

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.590
in orders of four, seven,

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.659
15, 20, and 30.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:07.760
Yes!

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:11.598
I don't know what maniac is at a Wingstop

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.834
and gets chicken tenders instead of wings.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.803
I mean, I get it if
you're taking your, like,

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.371
10-year-old there.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:21.007
Let's weigh five chicken
tenders here in the US.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:33.019
So, five plain tenders in
the UK weighs 230 grams.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.387
200 and what?

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.422
Way over 300 on this one.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.790
We're over 300,

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.360
and they try to pass this off as a tender.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.228
Bigger chunks of meat over here in the US.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:45.598
Bigger tender chunks of meat.

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:46.666
What about a side of fries?

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.668
Well, in the UK, these come in two sizes.

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:51.538
Regular

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:52.839
and large.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.975
And in the US, our Wingstop fries

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:57.777
also come in two sizes.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.445
Regular

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.748
and large.

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.183
How do those look?

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:05.151
Harry: We're gonna weigh them
both to see what they come to.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.389
[laughing]

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:13.193
That's not a good look for fries.

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:16.596
How do I get this back in?

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.638
Yep, also a brick.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.273
Also a brick.

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:32.011
Harry: And the large
portion came to 255 grams.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.847
Our regular is bigger than your large, UK.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:35.682
OK.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.355
Oh, lost a fry.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.790
400 grams.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:47.160
Fountain drinks in the
UK come in one size.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.361
It's 22 ounces.

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.897
But, unfortunately, we
weren't able to get one today.

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:52.031
Wingstop in the US, you can get

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.701
your fountain drinks in two sizes,

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.436
20 ounce

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:58.037
and

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.239
32 ounce.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.173
The Wingstop we went to

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:02.275
did not have any 32-ounce cups.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:04.344
Dips in the UK only come in one size,

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.278
and it's regular.

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:06.879
We're gonna weigh a cup of ranch

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:08.848
to see how much we get.

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:10.583
Dips in the US come in two sizes,

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.052
regular and this absurd tub.

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.220
Look at this.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.955
First we're gonna weigh this,

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:19.058
the regular size.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:19.993
Now the big boy.

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:22.929
I couldn't even guess how
much this container weighs.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.498
Before I do this?

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:26.766
Closer to 300.

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:28.067
This is heavy.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.969
This is like a half a bottle of ranch.

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:33.172
[laughing]

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.542
Bro!

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.811
It is 440.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:42.215
440 grams of ranch.

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.216
So, fun fact about me,

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:45.184
I've never actually had ranch before.

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:48.054
This is not a common dressing in the UK.

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:49.389
It's just not really on menus.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:52.692
We prefer, like, a garlic
mayonnaise or a ketchup.

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:55.028
So I'm about to try my first-ever ranch.

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:55.895
See how it goes.

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:01.834
[chicken crunching]

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:05.004
Hmm. OK. OK.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:07.040
I don't know if Wingstop ranch differs to

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.474
the classic ranch you
might find in the States,

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:09.375
but it's nice.

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:12.245
If you want, like, a kind of cooling thing

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:13.780
with a similar effect
to mayo in that regard,

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:16.549
but, like, a little bit more
tang, bit more seasoning.

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:18.384
Yeah, you guys are doing it well.

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.155
The biggest thing on the
menu in the UK is this,

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:23.923
the Flavour Craver wing platter.

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:26.926
You get 24 wings, three
dips, and no other sides.

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:29.796
All for a price of 22.50 pounds.

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:32.332
Biggest single menu item
at the Wingstop in the US

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:34.934
is this, the 100-wing party pack.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:37.303
OK, obviously you start with 100 wings.

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:39.038
You can get up to six different flavors.

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:40.473
I just got the same one.

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.375
Four orders of large fries.

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:44.143
Four orders of veggie sticks.

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:45.778
And eight dips.

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.814
This is supposed to feed 13 people.

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:49.949
Or, like, you and three of your friends.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.984
You can get boneless or bone-in wings.

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:55.254
If you go boneless it's $94.39,

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:59.759
and if you go all bone-in
wings it's $104.19.

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:02.428
I gotta say, I'm generally a
drums guy over a flats guy.

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:03.796
I think it's just the shape is great.

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:04.964
It's just like a meat lollipop.

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:06.399
And also it feels like you get more meat

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:08.034
on there than you do on a flat.

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:09.635
No, Harry, no.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:10.470
Drums are not good.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.537
Flats are way better.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:12.872
You can pull out both bones.

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.507
You get all the meat off of it.

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:16.809
For the drum, it's way
harder to get the meat off.

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:19.412
Don't be deceived by that
shape. It's less meat.

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.380
Flats.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.148
Flats!

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:23.883
I have a flat head.

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:26.386
[funky music]

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:28.955
Here is everything you will only find

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:30.957
on the menu at a UK Wingstop.

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:32.358
And here are all the exclusive items

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:34.927
you can get at a US Wingstop.

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:35.762
We'll start with the chicken.

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:37.363
There's actually one flavor of wing

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:39.232
that we can get that you guys can't,

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.099
which is this one,

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:42.702
it's Brazilian citrus pepper.

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:44.437
I'm gonna try the Brazilian citrus pepper

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:48.007
using my patented wing-eating technique.

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:49.409
Get one of the bones out.

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:51.144
And then a little meat lollipop.

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:54.213
Mm.

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:56.182
Nice little freshness from the citrus,

00:06:56.182 --> 00:06:58.184
kick from the pepper.

00:06:58.184 --> 00:06:59.018
Not bad.

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:00.920
So, for exclusive wing flavors,

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.054
you can get these two,

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:05.291
the Bayou BBQ and the lemon hot.

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:08.761
We can also get any
Wingstop flavor on the side.

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.263
I don't know if you
can get that in the UK.

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:13.299
Another thing you can
do at the US Wingstop

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:15.134
is you can customize your fries

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:17.703
or you can get regular or extra seasoning.

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:20.072
So I got an extra seasoning of a seasoning

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.541
you guys don't have in the UK,

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:23.075
which is the garlic Parmesan.

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:24.310
Look at the seasoning on this.

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:26.579
I mean, they just dusted
this thing, right?

00:07:26.579 --> 00:07:28.648
You know exactly what I'm gonna do.

00:07:28.648 --> 00:07:30.650
Yeah, yeah!

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:34.487
These are Louisiana Voodoo fries.

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:36.889
They are topped with a cheese sauce,

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:39.125
ranch, and Cajun seasoning.

00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:41.194
Our exclusive fry option is this.

00:07:42.061 --> 00:07:43.262
Sweet potato fries.

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:45.331
These come in sizes of regular or large,

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:46.966
and you can also get them
in the same seasonings

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:48.234
as the regular fries.

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:49.435
In my opinion, you guys aren't

00:07:49.435 --> 00:07:50.803
missing out on much with these.

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:52.638
I just always think
that sweet potato fries

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.073
are worse than regular fries.

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:56.609
They always cost more,
they always come out soggy.

00:07:56.609 --> 00:07:57.443
It's just not worth it.

00:07:57.443 --> 00:07:58.744
Just stay with the regular.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.182
Outside of meat and potato,

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:05.184
you can also get Cajun fried corn.

00:08:05.184 --> 00:08:06.118
Am I saying that right?

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:07.353
It's fried?

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:10.323
You can also get freshly baked rolls.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.693
Bread, baby. Bread.

00:08:13.693 --> 00:08:15.728
We also have one other
exclusive side, which is this.

00:08:15.728 --> 00:08:17.797
It's a honey mustard slaw.

00:08:17.797 --> 00:08:20.500
We can also get booze from our Wingstops.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:23.035
This comes in the form
of two types of beer.

00:08:23.035 --> 00:08:25.171
And usually we would be able
to get two types of wine,

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:26.739
however, due to a reduced menu,

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:28.341
currently they are not serving them.

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:30.510
The three drink options
you can get in the US are,

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.645
oddly enough, sweetened
and unsweetened tea.

00:08:32.645 --> 00:08:34.714
I don't know why we have
tea and the UK does not.

00:08:34.714 --> 00:08:36.349
And also you can get this

00:08:36.349 --> 00:08:40.486
52-fluid-ounce Simply Lemonade.

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:41.420
And finally, in the UK,

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.556
you can finish off your
meal with some churros.

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:46.726
These come in portions
of either six or 10.

00:08:46.726 --> 00:08:48.327
You have two crumb options,

00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:51.097
including Oreo or Lotus Biscoff.

00:08:51.097 --> 00:08:52.732
And then you can choose
from one of two sauces,

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:54.233
either a sweet milk

00:08:54.233 --> 00:08:55.935
or some dulce de leche caramel.

00:08:59.939 --> 00:09:00.773
Mm.

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:03.376
Delicious.

00:09:03.376 --> 00:09:04.310
What about desserts?

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.478
Here's one you can get in the US

00:09:05.478 --> 00:09:07.213
and not in the UK at a Wingstop,

00:09:07.213 --> 00:09:10.416
the triple chocolate chunk brownie.

00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:11.617
Did I say that in the right order?

00:09:11.617 --> 00:09:13.553
Producer: Uh-huh.
Joe: Fantastic.

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:15.121
I'm now gonna do something really stupid,

00:09:15.121 --> 00:09:17.290
which is attempt to eat the hottest wing

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:18.691
on the Wingstop menu,

00:09:18.691 --> 00:09:20.726
which is the Atomic wing.

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:22.295
These come with gloves,

00:09:22.295 --> 00:09:24.096
just to avoid getting it on your skin

00:09:24.096 --> 00:09:26.032
and then getting it in your eyes.

00:09:26.032 --> 00:09:29.068
I'm not good with spice,
one thing to note.

00:09:29.068 --> 00:09:30.102
Ah, man.

00:09:30.102 --> 00:09:31.237
I don't really want to do this,

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:33.272
but, hey, for the content.

00:09:33.272 --> 00:09:34.206
Cheers.

00:09:41.414 --> 00:09:42.848
Yep, it's immediate.

00:09:46.085 --> 00:09:47.253
Oh, man.

00:09:51.057 --> 00:09:53.492
Deep breaths, Harry, deep breaths.

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:55.728
If Harry's doing it, I'm doing it too.

00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:02.234
This is the hottest?

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:03.202
I'm not a tough guy with the heat.

00:10:03.202 --> 00:10:04.236
This is not that hot.

00:10:10.076 --> 00:10:11.510
Yeah.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:12.912
It's not that hot.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.151
Yeah, I'm starting to feel it.

00:10:21.821 --> 00:10:22.655
Ugh.

00:10:23.856 --> 00:10:25.524
Now my tongue's kind of starting to hurt.

00:10:27.526 --> 00:10:29.829
What's what they do on
the, on "Hot Ones," when --

00:10:29.829 --> 00:10:30.896
[coughs]

00:10:30.896 --> 00:10:32.999
[dramatic music]

00:10:32.999 --> 00:10:34.033
Ugh, yeah.

00:10:37.103 --> 00:10:38.771
Unfortunately, Wingstop doesn't disclose

00:10:38.771 --> 00:10:41.240
any of its nutritional
information in the UK.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.109
They do disclose the
nutritional information

00:10:43.109 --> 00:10:44.310
in the US, however.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:46.012
And there are some pretty
interesting takeaways.

00:10:46.012 --> 00:10:47.613
OK, let's start with this.

00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:50.583
The classic meal for one,
an eight-piece combo.

00:10:50.583 --> 00:10:53.319
I got four hot wings, four lemon pepper,

00:10:53.319 --> 00:10:56.022
regular fry, dip, regular Coke.

00:10:56.022 --> 00:11:00.059
This meal contains a
total of 1,595 calories,

00:11:00.059 --> 00:11:03.429
along with a lot of your daily
fat and sodium allowance.

00:11:03.429 --> 00:11:04.997
Interestingly, if you get the same meal

00:11:04.997 --> 00:11:06.599
but boneless wings instead,

00:11:06.599 --> 00:11:09.001
the calories go up to 1,711,

00:11:09.001 --> 00:11:10.569
roughly a 7% increase.

00:11:10.569 --> 00:11:12.471
Even more interestingly,
the sodium in the meal

00:11:12.471 --> 00:11:15.641
rockets up to 5,258 milligrams,

00:11:15.641 --> 00:11:18.477
which is 228% of your daily allowance.

00:11:18.477 --> 00:11:19.578
So it looks like boneless wings

00:11:19.578 --> 00:11:21.681
are way saltier than bone-in wings,

00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:24.183
but they do contain slightly less fat.

00:11:24.183 --> 00:11:26.519
What's the most calorific
wing at Wingstop in the US?

00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:30.122
That would be the boneless
garlic Parmesan wing,

00:11:30.122 --> 00:11:34.760
which clocks in at 112
calories for just one.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:35.995
The saltiest wing on the menu

00:11:35.995 --> 00:11:38.064
is the boneless original hot wing.

00:11:38.064 --> 00:11:39.765
Now, it's less calorific
than the garlic Parmesan,

00:11:39.765 --> 00:11:40.833
but just five of these

00:11:40.833 --> 00:11:43.335
is your entire daily sodium allowance.

00:11:43.335 --> 00:11:45.604
The tenders at Wingstop
are, as you might expect,

00:11:45.604 --> 00:11:46.872
more calorific than the wings.

00:11:46.872 --> 00:11:49.742
The most calorific flavor in the US?

00:11:49.742 --> 00:11:50.943
Garlic Parmesan.

00:11:50.943 --> 00:11:52.478
Where have I heard that before?

00:11:52.478 --> 00:11:53.913
That's not the saltiest tender.

00:11:53.913 --> 00:11:56.982
That crown goes to the Cajun spice tender,

00:11:56.982 --> 00:12:00.086
with 775 milligrams of sodium.

00:12:00.086 --> 00:12:03.022
Just three of these is your
entire daily allowance.

00:12:03.022 --> 00:12:05.624
I didn't come here to
not eat chicken tenders.

00:12:05.624 --> 00:12:06.459
Mm.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:10.262
[peppy music]

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.001
What about the dips?

00:12:16.001 --> 00:12:18.170
Well, the least healthy
dip on the menu is this.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:19.105
It's honey mustard.

00:12:19.105 --> 00:12:20.973
Just a regular portion of this in the US

00:12:20.973 --> 00:12:24.744
contains 367 calories, 33 grams of fat,

00:12:24.744 --> 00:12:26.512
5 grams of saturated fat,

00:12:26.512 --> 00:12:28.547
682 milligrams of sodium,

00:12:28.547 --> 00:12:31.183
and a slightly alarming 17 grams of sugar.

00:12:31.183 --> 00:12:32.551
As for the rest of the menu,

00:12:32.551 --> 00:12:34.353
you really wanna watch out for the fries.

00:12:34.353 --> 00:12:36.589
The most calorific single menu item

00:12:36.589 --> 00:12:39.358
on a Wingstop menu is a large portion

00:12:39.358 --> 00:12:41.794
of the Louisiana Voodoo fries.

00:12:41.794 --> 00:12:45.464
This serving alone, 910 calories,

00:12:45.464 --> 00:12:48.167
which is almost half of
your daily allowance.

00:12:48.167 --> 00:12:49.502
If you're looking to
cut down on the sodium,

00:12:49.502 --> 00:12:51.904
you might want to avoid
the Buffalo ranch fries.

00:12:51.904 --> 00:12:53.105
They're slightly less calorific

00:12:53.105 --> 00:12:54.473
than the Louisiana Voodoo fries;

00:12:54.473 --> 00:12:57.710
however, they contain
2,880 milligrams of sodium.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:00.813
That's 125% of your
entire daily allowance.

00:13:00.813 --> 00:13:02.581
In summary, Wingstop,

00:13:02.581 --> 00:13:04.784
maybe not the healthiest fast-food chain.

00:13:04.784 --> 00:13:06.752
If you're looking to
cut back on your sodium,

00:13:06.752 --> 00:13:08.754
definitely skip the boneless wings

00:13:08.754 --> 00:13:11.323
and maybe stick to regular fries,

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:13.926
and not the ones with
these gross toppings.

00:13:16.862 --> 00:13:18.264
Now, sadly, along with the nutrition,

00:13:18.264 --> 00:13:21.066
Wingstop UK also doesn't
disclose its ingredients.

00:13:21.066 --> 00:13:24.537
Wingstop also does not disclose
its ingredients in the US.

00:13:24.537 --> 00:13:26.305
[crickets chirping]

00:13:26.305 --> 00:13:28.774
So, what do we know about
what goes into the chicken?

00:13:28.774 --> 00:13:29.975
Well, for starters, in the UK,

00:13:29.975 --> 00:13:33.112
the chicken is not organic
and not free-range.

00:13:33.112 --> 00:13:35.281
All the chicken they use
in the UK is also halal,

00:13:35.281 --> 00:13:37.750
which means it's suitable
for Muslim people to eat.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:39.919
Now, it is unclear if the US chickens

00:13:39.919 --> 00:13:41.654
are free-range or organic.

00:13:41.654 --> 00:13:44.390
All Wingstops say that they
expect their chicken supplier

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:46.959
to conform with USDA, FDA,

00:13:46.959 --> 00:13:48.761
state, and local regulations.

00:13:48.761 --> 00:13:50.663
However, they do not specify a grading.

00:13:50.663 --> 00:13:53.232
So for all we know it
could be grade C chicken,

00:13:53.232 --> 00:13:56.535
which can be misshapen, poorly fleshed,

00:13:56.535 --> 00:13:58.003
and, Jesus,

00:13:58.003 --> 00:14:01.440
and with no limit on the
size, number of areas,

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:05.778
or intensity of discolorations
and flesh bruises.

00:14:05.778 --> 00:14:07.880
Wow, I wish I knew that a few minutes ago.

00:14:08.981 --> 00:14:10.249
In better news, the fact that

00:14:10.249 --> 00:14:12.351
they refer to their tenders as "tenders"

00:14:12.351 --> 00:14:14.887
legally means that they have to at least

00:14:14.887 --> 00:14:17.389
be made of whole cuts of chicken breast

00:14:17.389 --> 00:14:20.125
and might be actual chicken tenderloins,

00:14:20.125 --> 00:14:22.628
which are in the inner pectoral muscles

00:14:22.628 --> 00:14:24.430
of the chicken breast.

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:25.798
And that's pretty much all we can glean

00:14:25.798 --> 00:14:28.033
from the information
that's publicly available.

00:14:28.033 --> 00:14:30.803
Why are you so sneaky, Wingstop?

00:14:30.803 --> 00:14:33.772
Is it because you know
we'll eat it regardless?

00:14:33.772 --> 00:14:35.374
Correct.

00:14:35.374 --> 00:14:36.642
Ooh, I f---ed up.

00:14:38.444 --> 00:14:40.512
I should've waited before I
went into that second wing.

00:14:40.512 --> 00:14:41.447
[laughs]

00:14:41.447 --> 00:14:42.248
[exhales]

